                "file": "src/Lending.Host/Cli/CommandLine.fs",
                "line": 164,
                "quote": "if Accounts.owed (MemberId m) library >= 5.00m then"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The waiver rules (approver required, choosing the earliest unpaid fine for the copy, PaidAtWaiver, no further payments, owed excluding waived fines) are all in Tier 1/2. Tier 3 re-derives the waived/partly-paid status and the 'settled' predicate, which agrees with Tier 2. The borrow-blocking decision is still made in the Tier 4 CLI against a hard-coded 5.00m. That was already there, but the change touched the line and left the decision in Tier 4.",
            "score": 1
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Host/Cli/CommandLine.fs",
                "line": 164,
                "quote": "if Accounts.owed (MemberId m) library >= 5.00m then"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The change rewrites the borrow branch of the Tier 4 presentation module so that it calls `Accounts.owed`, a Tier 2 function, directly. That is a new violation of ARC-BND-02, where presentation re-enters Tier 2 decisions. The earlier inline arithmetic was also a violation, but this edit adds a Host-to-Tier-2 call and keeps the blocking decision in Tier 4. The new waive path and the persistence changes correctly go through UseCases and the existing Store port.",
